WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-Welcome to the show, everybody.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:04.467
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
You're here.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
You made it.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.000
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.467
Guys, it is Groundhog Day.
Yeah.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.968
[ Cheers ]

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:14.367
That's right, this morning,
Punxsutawney Phil predicted

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:17.067
six more weeks of classified
documents being found.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.801
Actually, Punxsutawney Phil

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.067
predicted six more weeks
of winter.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.200
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
But I read --

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.801
I read that he's only right
40% of the time.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:28.701
When they heard that,
weather.com was like,

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.033
"You're hired.
When can you start?"

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.033
Yeah, you can't trust
Punxsutawney Phil.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.267
He's basically the George Santos
of the groundhog world.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.767
Meanwhile, in New York,
we've got a groundhog

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.534
named Staten Island Chuck.

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:43.634
[ Cheers ]
You know him? Yeah.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:46.734
And he --
he predicted an early spring.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:52.434
Well, technically he predicted
an "early friggin' spring."

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.834
Yep, Staten Island Chuck
hits it a little different.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.267
He just comes out
with his robe open,

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.200
grabs the paper,
and goes back inside.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.200
"How's your sister doing?
All right, hey."

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.467
Well, this morning up in Canada,
they held a celebration

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.868
with their own groundhog,
named Fred,

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.534
but things didn't go as planned.

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.200
This is real.
Take a look.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:24.934
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.434
[ Sad tuba ]

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:30.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:32.834
-Not Fred.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.534
-Every parent is like,
"What are you doing?

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.534
Just buy another groundhog
and say it's Fred!"

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:37.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:40.300
"Look how great -- look how
great Fred looks today.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.901
He looks fantastic."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.701
"Fred, he has blond hair now.
It's unbelievable."

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:47.634
-That's not --
-Why would you do that?

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.033
Now I'm just worried
that they'll never know

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:52.133
if it's gonna be cold in Canada.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.801
Who knows what happened to Fred?

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.834
Staten Island Chuck was like,
"I didn't see nothin'."

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.868
"Don't worry 'bout it.
Hey, is your sister good?

00:01:58.868 --> 00:01:59.868
All right."

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:04.300
Switching -- Switching gears,
you guys see this last night?

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.567
White House chief of staff
Ron Klain

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:08.234
officially stepped down.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.534
And during his farewell speech,
he got a little emotional.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:11.601
Check it out.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.501
-I will try to keep this brief,

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.667
but I cannot promise
there will not be some tears.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:18.901
[ Voice breaking ] This is
the best job I've ever had.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:22.167
And for dead again,
in the winter of 2020

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.701
and for dead again
in the winter of 2021.

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:26.834
I'm often asked,
"What is the best souvenir

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:29.334
I got in two years
as White House chief of staff?"

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:30.734
[ Voice breaking ]
It's this rock.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:33.200
[ Laughter ]
This plain, and simple rock.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:37.701
-Aww.

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:39.200
-Biden was like, "I think
we made the right call.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.501
Someone get him into --"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:44.167
"Let's get him into --
get you an Uber right now."

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.534
-He's busted up over Fred.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.400
-He was only there two years.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.067
Tom Brady was in football
for 23 seasons.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.300
This guy...
I don't know.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.501
This is going viral, though.
Today, Pope Francis

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:58.434
posted a tweet, and then, a few
minutes later, he deleted it,

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:00.367
and I think you'll
understand why. He said...

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:12.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.801
Meanwhile, God was like,
"Jesus Christ..."

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:16.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:18.868
"Get him off Twitter.
Get him into an Uber."

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.100
Some business news --
Netflix is about to start

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.434
cracking down
on password sharing.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.934
[ Crowd booing ]
Yeah.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:30.701
They're gonna limit sharing
to one household.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.167
People --
[ Crowd booing ]

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:34.868
People are upset.
I mean, "Never Have I Ever"

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.200
been this outraged.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:39.334
I'm "Blown Away."

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:42.067
You're telling me I can't share
an account with a "Stranger?"

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.868
"Things" are out of control.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:50.567
Netflix, what
"Maid" "You" do this?

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:52.734
I can't think
of a "Dahmer" idea.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.801
This really takes "The Crown."

00:03:56.801 --> 00:04:01.634
You're telling me I have to
"Lupin" every "Watcher"

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:05.934
on my account, including my
friend "Emily in Paris"?

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:09.934
And say,
"I Think you Should Leave."

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:11.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:14.200
What "A Series
of Unfortunate Events."

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.000
Sure I could pay extra,
but I'm already paying too much

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.968
for "Coco, melons," eggs.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.701
Also, who knows
when this takes effect.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:23.334
It could be tomorrow.
It could be --

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:25.200
could be next "Wednesday."

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.334
Or tonight at "Midnight.
Mass" panic is setting in.

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:31.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.667
So, Netflix, this is the
"Last Chance U" have

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:38.868
before I build a "Bridgerton"-el

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:41.634
to your headquarters
and tell you in person,

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.601
"You're 'Dead To Me.'"

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:44.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:48.501
♪♪

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:55.000
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.767
"This little rock --"

00:04:56.767 --> 00:05:01.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.834
Guys, get this --
Tomorrow, the movie

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.701
"80 for Brady" comes out,
which --

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:06.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.601
...which Tom Brady stars in,
and he suggested that

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:11.934
there could be more acting
in his future.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:14.234
Yeah, Brady's a very good actor
'cause right now we all believe

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.701
that he's actually gonna retire.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.767
Some more entertainment news --
I saw that Tom Hanks is filming

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:22.200
a new movie that's using
artificial intelligence

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.167
to de-age him
and make him look younger.

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:26.868
It's -- It's amazing
what they can do now.

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:29.501
Just look at what happens when
you use A.I. to de-age someone.

00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:31.968
For instance,
here's King Charles, okay?

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.667
If you de-age him,
you get Cap'n Crunch.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.267
And it's like --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.400
It's amazing technology.
-Wow.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.734
-Amazing.
-Fantastic.

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:41.133
-Here, Pope Francis --
here's Pope Francis.

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.968
You de-age him,
you get Timothée Chalamet.

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:46.167
And it's just --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:48.467
It's an amazing -- here --
here's Patrick Mahomes.

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:51.667
If you de-age him you get
Richie from "Family Matters."

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:55.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:56.968
Next, here's the old guy
from "Up."

00:05:56.968 --> 00:06:00.100
If you de-age him,
you get George Santos.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:01.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:03.601
It's -- It's happening.
I mean, the future is here.

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:05.467
Here's Eagles center
Jason Kelce.

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:06.501
-Yeah?
-If you de-age him,

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:08.133
you get Buzz from "Home Alone."

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:10.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.000
Next, here's President Biden.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.667
If you de-age him,
you get Bob Barker.

00:06:14.667 --> 00:06:16.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:17.234
[ Rim shot ]

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:18.734
-Wow!

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:25.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.367
-And finally --
finally, here's Tom Brady.

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:30.901
If you de-age him,
you get Tom Brady.

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:32.701
[ Laughter and applause ]
Doesn't need A.I.

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:36.100
Good-looking dude.
He doesn't need it.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.234
Finally, police in Massachusetts
are looking for

00:06:38.234 --> 00:06:42.000
a 200-pound Shrek sculpture
that was stolen.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.901
This is real.
Can we see a photo of the --

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:47.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.634
Looks like a cake someone made
on "Nailed It."

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:51.767
Even the sculptor was like,

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:53.167
"I can't believe
someone stole that."

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.467
We have --
We have a great show tonight.

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.267
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:06:57.267 --> 00:06:59.501
-♪ People know my city
gotta mesmerize ♪

00:06:59.501 --> 00:07:01.901
♪ Block away in a house
from the 2-1-5 ♪

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:05.000
♪ To beat poetry
would be my every day ♪

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:09.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.067
-Oh, my goodness!
-Come on.

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:12.667
-We have a big show tonight.
-Oh.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:15.334
-Big show tonight.
Tomorrow, though,

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.000
for the first time ever --
very interesting --

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.634
for the first time ever,
The Roots will not be

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.200
the house band
for "The Tonight Show."

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.467
-Whoa.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:07:22.467 --> 00:07:23.934
-Yeah.
-They didn't know that?

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:25.033
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.033 --> 00:07:26.234
[ Voice breaking ]
And they got a --

00:07:26.234 --> 00:07:28.167
I gave them a little rock
to take --

00:07:28.167 --> 00:07:29.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:31.934
For the -- they actually --
Can we say what you're --

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:33.801
what you're doing?
-Yeah, you can say it.

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:37.367
-You're part of a giant
performance at The Grammys.

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:42.100
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:46.100
-50 --
50 years of hip hop.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.000
-Yeah.
-And you guys are in charge

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.501
of all -- you'll be playing
with a bunch of --

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:52.367
-A lot of people.
-Yeah.

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:53.968
Should I say --
Can I say of these names?

00:07:53.968 --> 00:07:55.300
-You can say some, yeah.
-I can?

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.901
-Yeah.
-I can say Busta Rhymes?

00:07:56.901 --> 00:07:58.334
-You can say it.
[ Cheers ]

00:07:58.334 --> 00:08:00.801
-I can say Missy Elliott?
-Can't say that.

00:08:00.801 --> 00:08:02.000
-Can't say that.
[ Cheers ]

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.133
-Can I say Grandmaster Flash?

00:08:03.133 --> 00:08:04.234
-Oh, yeah.
-Sure, sure.

00:08:04.234 --> 00:08:05.734
-You can say it.
-Can I say Ice-T?

00:08:05.734 --> 00:08:06.834
-Yeah.
[ Cheers ]

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:08.267
-Can I say Lil Wayne?
-Yeah.

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:09.267
[ Cheers ]

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:11.667
-Can I say Public Enemy?!
-What?!

00:08:11.667 --> 00:08:14.300
-Can I say Queen Latifah?!
-Whoa!

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.467
-Can I say Run-D.M.C.?!

00:08:16.467 --> 00:08:18.767
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:18.767 --> 00:08:21.300
-Dude, that's gonna be massive.
-It is.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.634
-I'm very excited about that.
It's cool.

00:08:22.634 --> 00:08:24.868
And, also, are you still doing
your Grammy party?

00:08:24.868 --> 00:08:26.200
-Yeah, yep.
-Is that the night --

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:27.567
-I forgot, yes, we are.
-The night before.

00:08:27.567 --> 00:08:30.300
-You have that, as well.
Gosh, you're busy this weekend.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.534
So, anyways, we're going,
"Well, who --

00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:35.501
who should be the band
for our -- for our show?"

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:37.467
Our first time -- we've never
had to think of

00:08:37.467 --> 00:08:39.334
who would be here if The Roots
weren't here.

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:41.601
And I was like, my first thing
that came to my mind is,

00:08:41.601 --> 00:08:44.367
"I wonder if he would do it,
but could we get Paul Shaffer

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:46.834
to come back to the building?"

00:08:46.834 --> 00:08:49.367
And I called Paul Shaffer,
and he said yes.

00:08:49.367 --> 00:08:50.801
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:54.767
-Paul Shaffer and
the World's Most Dangerous Band

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:57.834
are back at NBC after 30 years.

00:08:57.834 --> 00:08:59.467
I cannot wait.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:59.467 --> 00:09:02.133
I love Paul.
Everyone's coming.

00:09:02.133 --> 00:09:05.534
Felicia, Anton.
It's gonna be fantastic.

00:09:05.534 --> 00:09:07.267
I'm so excited about that.

00:09:07.267 --> 00:09:08.734
Guys, we have a great show
for you tonight.

00:09:08.734 --> 00:09:11.501
He stars in the giant new show
"The Last of Us,"

00:09:11.501 --> 00:09:14.267
which airs Sundays
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:09:14.267 --> 00:09:16.767
And he is hosting
"Saturday Night Live"

00:09:16.767 --> 00:09:19.601
this weekend,
with musical guest Coldplay --

00:09:19.601 --> 00:09:23.601
Pedro Pascal is here!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:23.601 --> 00:09:26.000
He's good dude.
-A lovely man.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.501
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:09:27.501 --> 00:09:31.467
-Plus, you can see her
in the new movie

00:09:31.467 --> 00:09:33.901
"Ant-Man and The Wasp:
Quantumania,"

00:09:33.901 --> 00:09:36.767
which is in theaters and IMAX
February 17th --

00:09:36.767 --> 00:09:39.100
Kathryn Newton is here tonight!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:42.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:42.367 --> 00:09:45.767
And we got great music
from Armani White!

00:09:45.767 --> 00:09:48.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.667
He's real good.
Fantastic.

00:09:51.667 --> 00:09:53.667
History of hip hop.
This dude --

00:09:53.667 --> 00:09:56.234
This guy's gonna be on the list.

00:09:56.234 --> 00:10:00.133
Apparently, guys, the FDA
is going to regulate CBD.

00:10:00.133 --> 00:10:01.367
-Really?
-Yeah, I heard -- yeah.

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:06.601
And there's a new form of A.I.
called ChatGPT.

00:10:06.601 --> 00:10:09.467
And then people are wondering
who's gonna be the NFL MVP.

00:10:09.467 --> 00:10:11.868
There's a lot of acronyms...
-Floating in the air.

00:10:11.868 --> 00:10:13.167
-...floating in the news,

00:10:13.167 --> 00:10:14.634
including some
you might not know about.

00:10:14.634 --> 00:10:16.467
This is "Acronym News."

00:10:16.467 --> 00:10:17.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:20.868
-♪ Acronym News,
Acronym News ♪

00:10:20.868 --> 00:10:22.667
♪ Yeah, yeah ♪

00:10:22.667 --> 00:10:25.000
-Now, I didn't know this,
but it turns out Brady

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.501
